    "node_id": "C_kwDOACN7MtoAKDRkZDEwZmJiZWI5YzMzNzA5ZWRjODk5MTZlMTljMDNjNzgwYTA3NTE",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Kees Cook",
        "email": "kees+treewide@kernel.org",
        "date": "2026-10-29T06:16:33Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Kees Cook",
        "email": "kees@kernel.org",
        "date": "2026-11-06T05:55:50Z"
      },
      "message": "treewide: Convert devm_kmalloc() family to the devm_kmalloc_obj() family\n\nMirroring the earlier kmalloc_obj() conversion, convert the\ndevice-managed allocators over to the type-based API using the now\nupdated scripts/coccinelle/api/kmalloc_objs.cocci. The size is derived\nfrom the type rather than written out as a sizeof(), and the result is\na pointer to that type rather than void *, so a mismatch between the\nsize requested and the variable assigned becomes a build error instead\nof being silently accepted.\n\nThe conversions break down as:\n\n\t6713\tdevm_kzalloc_obj()\n\t1749\tdevm_kzalloc_objs()\n\t 307\tdevm_kzalloc_flex()\n\t  91\tdevm_kmalloc_objs()\n\t  82\tdevm_kmalloc_obj()\n\t   2\tdevm_kmalloc_flex()\n\nThe rules deliberately leave alone allocations sized by a string or a\nbyte-sized type, or assigned to a pointer to a byte-sized type, since\nthose are byte buffers rather than objects. Allocations sized by a\nmulti-byte integer type are only converted when they are assigned to a\npointer to that same type, and allocations of pointers to integers or of\nvoid pointers are left alone too. After this change, 528 files still\ncall devm_kmalloc(), devm_kzalloc(), devm_kcalloc(), or\ndevm_kmalloc_array().\n\nBuild tested with allmodconfig on x86_64, arm64, i386, arm, riscv, s390,\nm68k, mips, parisc, sparc, loongarch, arc, xtensa, and openrisc with GCC\n16.2.0 with no new warnings.\n\nSigned-off-by: Kees Cook <kees+treewide@kernel.org>",
